#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Context Integrity Gate (CIG) — Expert-level, deterministic, zero-trust context intake.

What it does:
- Accepts raw context (dict / JSON string / JSON file)
- Canonicalizes data (stable internal representation)
- Validates (schema + invariants + safe JSON rules)
- Enforces policy (blocklist / secret-field detection / size limits)
- Produces an explainable decision: ACCEPT | REJECT | FLAG
- Persists audit events safely (atomic write + lock + optional rotation)

No AI. No guessing. No bypass.

Run:
  python cig.py --help
  python cig.py --input-json '{"schema_version":1,"context_type":"profile","subject":{"id":"u1","kind":"user"},"attributes":{"name":"  john  doe  "}}' --source api
  python cig.py --run-tests

Tip:
- Start with the default schema/policy below, then customize the RULES section for your domain.
"""

